course: dictionary
lesson: 10532
title: What does UFO really mean?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A UFO is short for «unidentified flying object». Unidentified means nobody has worked out what the object is yet. It does not mean it is an alien. Most things people see in the sky turn out to be planes, satellites, weather balloons, drones or planets.
explain: The sentence «From the Earth it is the brightest thing in the night sky after the Moon, so bright that people sometimes report it as a UFO.» is probably describing the planet Venus. People who do not know what they are looking at can think a bright light is strange, but it is not a spaceship.
explain: Think like a scientist. When you see something you cannot explain, look for the most likely answer first, and only then consider stranger ideas. Governments now often use the term UAP (unidentified anomalous phenomena) for the same idea. In films and stories, UFOs often bring aliens to Earth, but that is fiction, not proof.
fact: UFO is short for «unidentified flying object».
fact: «Unidentified» means not yet explained or named, not proven to be alien.
fact: Most UFO sightings turn out to be planes, satellites, weather balloons, drones, planets like Venus, or tricks of light.
fact: Scientists say there is no confirmed evidence that aliens have visited Earth.
fact: In films and stories, a UFO often means a flying saucer, an alien spaceship.
exercise: What does UFO stand for? | unknown fizzing orbit | unusual fast object | *unidentified flying object | underwater flying oven
exercise: «From the Earth it is the brightest thing in the night sky after the Moon.» What is the most likely thing people report as a UFO here? | a cloud shaped like a cat | *a bright planet like Venus | a school bus flying over the park | a car with its headlights on
exercise: Why does «unidentified» not mean «alien»? | It means it is definitely from another planet | It means it is a type of weather | *It means nobody has explained it yet | It means it is a film prop
test: Which is NOT a common explanation for a UFO sighting? | a drone | *a dragon | a satellite | a weather balloon
test: What do scientists say about aliens visiting Earth? | *There is no confirmed evidence that they have | They visit every week in planes | They have proof from every sighting | They have never been asked
exam: Governments now often use which term for UFOs? | UFP | *UAP | UFS | UFA
